/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Measure delay in units of τ, the delay of an ideal inverter driving an identical inverter with no parasitic capacitance (about 3RC for a unit transistor of resistance R and gate capacitance C).
   - h = Cout/Cin is the electrical effort (often called fan-out), g the logical effort, f = gh the stage effort and p the parasitic delay, all in units of τ or dimensionless.
   - Logical effort g is how much more input capacitance a gate needs than an inverter to deliver the same output current.
   - Parasitic delay p is the delay from the gate's own diffusion capacitance, roughly proportional to the number of transistors on its output node.
   - For a path of N stages, define the path logical effort G = g1g2…gN and the path electrical effort H = Cload/Cin,path.
   - The product of the stage efforts is fixed at F, so their sum is least when all are equal (the arithmetic mean is never below the geometric mean).
   - D = N F1/N + P, P = p1 + … + pN Here d is the path delay in τ.
   - The number of stages can be chosen too.
   - This is often called path delay optimisation or the method of logical effort.
*/
